From 71cc14dc9132994c6f494ba9c073d791eaea7bfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: salvia420-bit <salvia420@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:40:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/29] fix(economy): Tier 5 adversarial fixes across siege,
 cold-chain, till caps, inventory overflow & wire guards

- [CRIT-01] GameActionVehicle DepositSupply (0x0912 Action=2) now locates and consumes physical server-side supply cargo/container/inventory units and derives authoritative OriginLandblockId and SupplyPoints instead of trusting client fields.
- [CRIT-02] SiegeManager requires liveRingHolder in 30m ring to advance ClaimElapsedSec/BreachElapsedSec, resets unheld claim/breach timers, and extends KeepSiegedLandblockActive to active claim/breach states.
- [HIGH-01] WorldObject_Tick passes PerishableDecay.IsInsidePoweredReefer(this, null) so world-placed perishables inside powered Reefers freeze at 0.0x decay.
- [HIGH-02] TownEconomyManager persists/restores TownTillCapPyreals across Initialize(), inherits TownTillCapPyreals in GetOrCreateLedgerLocked, and enforces regularPayout <= TownTillCapPyreals in mixed Trade-Note sales.
- [HIGH-03] Player_Inventory trophy turn-in, AgentGatewayService fulfill_order, and IndustryManager.TryMintBullion pre-check capacity and roll back atomically on full inventory instead of burning Pyreals or bullion.
- [HIGH-04] GameActionVehicle WithdrawEscrow (0x0912 Action=4) genuinely withdraws spendable funds via TownEconomyManager, delivers Pyreal stacks with full-inventory rollback, persists, and broadcasts state.
- [MED-09..11, LOW-01] Fixed 16-bit cross-continent origin distance/provenance, non-finite GeologyService positions, HandleLogisticsConvoyOrder CapObserve gate, and 53-bit safe JS bounds on order_id/convoy_id.
- Added Tier 5 adversarial C# tests (EconomyE2E 45/45, Economy|VehicleWire 154/154, Vehicles|Landblock 367/367 Debug passing).
